atari800: output mono POKEY to both channels

PLATFORM_SoundSetup() forced 2 channels whatever the core asked for.
Sound_Setup() hands that count to POKEYSND_Init() as the number of
POKEY chips, so in the default mono mode (atari800_pokey_stereo
disabled: Sound_desired.channels = 1) the core emulated a second POKEY
that nothing writes. The left channel carried the game, the right
channel was silence, and retro_sound_update()'s mono path (copy the
one channel to both) never ran.

Found on the GPi Case 2, whose speaker plays the right channel: Atari
800 was the only silent system there, while HDMI (stereo TV) still
played it from the left side. Probably also why this core sounded weak
on the Orange Pi Zero3.

Keep the requested channel count: 1 normally, 2 with the stereo POKEY
option on (two real POKEYs, as before).

Signed-off-by: RetroArch-PI
--- a/libretro/platform.c
+++ b/libretro/platform.c
@@ -1036,10 +1036,15 @@
 
 int PLATFORM_SoundSetup(Sound_setup_t *setup)
 {
-	//force 16 bit stereo sound at 44100
+	/* 16 bit at 44100. Keep the requested channel count (1 unless the
+	   atari800_pokey_stereo option is on): Sound_Setup() passes it to
+	   POKEYSND_Init() as the number of POKEYs, so forcing 2 emulated a
+	   second, never-written POKEY in the right channel and left mono
+	   games in the left channel only. */
 	setup->freq=44100;
 	setup->sample_size=2;
-	setup->channels=2;
+	if (setup->channels < 1 || setup->channels > 2)
+		setup->channels = 1;
 //	setup->buffer_ms=20;
 	setup->buffer_frames = 1024;
 
